\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every elliptic curve E over Q, does the mean of the analytic ranks of $E^{d}$, over nonzero signed squarefree d with $|d|<=X$, tend to one half as X tends to infinity?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every elliptic curve E over Q, does the mean of the analytic ranks of $E^{d}$, over nonzero signed squarefree d with $|d|<=X$, tend to one half as X tends to infinity?

