\section*{Mean analytic rank of quadratic twists over Q}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 006; 2026-09-23), the asserted result is that the mean analytic rank of signed squarefree quadratic twists tends to $1/2$ for each rational elliptic curve.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 006; 2026-09-23), block mollifiers compare twist families with a finite independent model. Poisson summation and an auxiliary square multiplier send dual twists to smaller height, allowing induction on logarithmic second moments and control of the contribution from large ranks.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 006; 2026-09-23).

